  "expectationsBeforeClassifierEdit": [
    "Product supplied is a labelled approximation of petroleum consumption; never production or sales. Crude supplied is direct fuel use on leases/pipelines, not refinery input consumption.",
    "Crude and petroleum products combined is the broad stock/consumption candidate; finished products, grades and individual fuels remain components. Weekly total petroleum products supplied is EIA headline consumption basis; prefer broader compatible total if published at requested frequency.",
    "Total gasoline stocks include finished gasoline and blending components. Finished gasoline alone is a component of stock totals; finished motor gasoline supplied is whole motor-gasoline consumption. Never add components to invent totals.",
    "Biofuels including fuel ethanol stock total is labelled liquid-biofuel stock basis; ethanol/biodiesel/renewable diesel/other biofuels alone remain components. Biofuel products supplied excludes refinery/blender inputs included in broader MER consumption and remains narrower.",
    "Stocks include SPR where EIA total publishes it. Excluding SPR, stocks at one facility type, in-transit, lease-only and component products cannot displace broader totals. Preserve EIA survey exclusions and historical scope changes.",
    "Prime supplier sales are sales for local consumption, not observed consumption. All-grade gasoline may qualify for sales with prime-supplier scope label under standing rule, subject to broader total preference. Individual refiner sales channels remain narrower than all supplier sales.",
